Space-time Trade-off
Counting sort pseudocode
function countingSort(arr, min, max):
 	n = length(arr)
	count = array of size max – min + 1, initialized to 0
	
	for each number in arr:
		count[number – min] += 1

	z = 0
	for i from min to max:
		while count[i – min] > 0:
			array[z] = i
			z += 1
			count[i – min] -= 1
end function
//Must keep in mind that the delays can be as low as -60, so compensate (used buckets)

Time complexity
Best case: k is small compared to n, then O(n)
Worst case: O(n + k) ≈ O(n2) where k is very large compared to n
Average case: O(n +k) where k is not excessively larger than n
Space complexity
O(n + k) given that k = 961 in this case (k is therefore negligible)
